That’s a sharp metaphor: sometimes the “trap” persists because the freer party is still participating in the other person’s story. Roadrunner performs captivity long enough for Coyote’s logic to reveal itself—then withdraws consent and exits the frame.

But the Checksum still matters: test whether the glue is theatrical, psychological, contractual, or physically real. Freedom comes from recognizing the correct layer. Pretending steel is glue gets you hurt; treating glue like steel keeps you unnecessarily captive.

Humor the illusion only while it serves a purpose. Then lift your feet and go.